2. Server data and artwork: owners keep their rights, Beezy gets a licence
==============================================================================

Applies to: everything under servers/ (metadata.json files and images) and to the
same material as it appears in built output (dist/).

This material is NOT licensed under MIT. Server names, descriptions, logos, banners,
backgrounds and wordmarks remain the property of their respective owners, and names
and logos may be trademarks.

By submitting material to this repository (for example with a pull request), the
contributor confirms that they own it or are authorised by the server's owner to submit
it, and grants Beezy Client a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence, which may
be revoked for the future by removing the material from this repository, to:

  - store, reproduce, resize, re-encode and crop the material;
  - display it in Beezy Client software (launcher, game client, website) and in services
    integrated with it, such as Discord Rich Presence;
  - distribute it to Beezy users as part of Beezy's server catalogue,

solely to identify and present the server. Beezy may keep copies it has already
distributed to users when material is removed, and may refuse or remove any material.

Anyone else may read and fork this repository, but may use material under servers/ only
as far as the law allows without permission from its owners (for example to identify a
server by name). Displaying the artwork in another product requires the owner's
permission, not Beezy's.

Inclusion in this repository does not mean Beezy endorses, sponsors or is affiliated
with any server, nor that any server endorses Beezy.
